{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Mirror inventory finding F14 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), LOW.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe 17 confirmable mutation verbs appear in three places:\n\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py:680` `_CONFIRM_SCOPE` — derived, canonical\n- `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py:43-46` `EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE`, emitted into `docs/cli-reference.md:8`\n- `docs/user-guide.md:27` — hand-authored, the same 17 backticked names\n\nAll three agree at 17/17 today, so this is preventive. The existing gate misses BOTH prose copies:\n\n- `_check_mutation_verbs()` (`gen_cli_reference.py:193`) compares the `MUTATION_VERBS` dict KEYS to\n  `_CONFIRM_SCOPE` — not the preamble.\n- `lint_editorial`'s route rule fires only on `rebar <verb>` forms, and the preamble uses bare\n  backticks.\n- `docs/user-guide.md` has no gate at all.\n\nSo adding a `confirmable=True` route updates the canonical set and the dict, and both prose copies\ngo stale silently — in exactly the documents that tell an agent which commands ask for confirmation.\n\n## Approach — add-parity-check\n\nExtend `_check_mutation_verbs` to parse the backticked verb list out of `EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE` and\nout of `docs/user-guide.md:27`, and compare both to `_CONFIRM_SCOPE`.\n\nParsing prose is the right move here rather than generating it: both passages are written as\nsentences with rationale, not as a bare list, and generating them would flatten guidance a reader\ndepends on. The check therefore asserts the SET matches while leaving the wording to a human.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `_check_mutation_verbs` compares the preamble's backticked verbs to `_CONFIRM_SCOPE` and\n      fails on any difference. Verified by a mutation adding a verb to the preamble and seeing RED.\n- [ ] AC2: it does the same for the `docs/user-guide.md` list. Verified by the equivalent mutation.\n- [ ] AC3: the failure names which document and which verbs, in which direction. Verified by\n      asserting the message content in both mutation checks.\n- [ ] AC4: both prose copies pass on the committed tree, i.e. the check is green at rest and the\n      17/17 agreement is confirmed rather than assumed. Verified by running the generator's checks.\n- [ ] AC5: the existing dict-keys comparison is retained, not replaced. Verified by the original\n      assertion still being present and exercised.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` — AC1-AC5 on the committed tree.\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"cli_reference or mutation_verbs or editorial\" -q`.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788385021587212001,"uuid":"c66a1632-d3ac-442e-97cf-89bad4e8fa1f"}